  "question": {
    "text": "Five charges $+q,+5 q,-2 q,+3 q$ and $-4 q$ are situated as shown in the figure. The electric flux due to this configuration through the surface $S$ is :\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0053_9ef1c22837d2.png\"><br>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{4 q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{5 q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3 q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "As per gauss theorem,\n$\\begin{aligned}& \\phi=\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_{\\text {in }}}{\\epsilon_0}=\\frac{\\mathrm{q}+(-2 \\mathrm{q})+5 \\mathrm{q}}{\\epsilon_0} \\\\\n& \\frac{4 \\mathrm{q}}{\\epsilon_0}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}